+# Agent Note: Session row-menu extension slot
+
+Status: implemented
+
+## Problem
+
+The Workspace browser's session `...` menu hardcodes Rename/Fork/Archive. A composed plugin (for example a copy-session-id action) has no additive seat: `sidebar.workspaces` is a `single` slot, so the only existing route is replacing the whole browsing region.
+
+## Decision
+
+`Menu` gains an optional `extra` ReactNode rendered after its ordinary items inside the list box, and `WorkspaceBrowser` declares a root-scoped `list` slot `sidebar.workspaces.session-menu` rendered into that region. Each session row passes the addressed `sessionId`, display `title`, and an `onClose` callback through the slot owner props. Contributions render their own menu cells (primitives stay importable platform modules), so no ReactNode crosses an inject or service boundary.
+
+Slot composition is the only extension path: no new client service, no menu-item registry, no ui-workspace API surface beyond the slot contract.
+
+## Alternatives considered
+
+- **Session row-menu action registry service** — rejected because it would expose ReactNode icons and labels through an inject face or a service snapshot, violating the slot-only composition and JSON-sharing rules in packages/client/AGENTS.md.
+- **Replacing `sidebar.workspaces` wholesale** — rejected because the browsing region is a `single` slot; a plugin re-implementing it must vendor the whole tree and drift with every upstream change.
+- **Reusing the existing footer/list slots** — rejected because the requirement is an item inside the per-row popover, not an extra button in the sidebar foot or row.
+
+## Consequences
+
+- `packages/client/ui-primitives`: `Menu.extra?: ReactNode`, inert when absent.
+- `packages/client/ui-workspace`: new SlotMap entry and declaration, renderSlot threading through `WorkspaceBrowser`/`SessionTree`/`SessionNodeItem`.
+- Empty slot renders nothing; existing menus are byte-identical otherwise.
+- Follow-ups: regenerate `packages/extensions/cordis-client-runner/src/client/slot-catalog.ts` via `pnpm run gen-client-catalog`, update `test:gui` coverage for the new render path, and run `DSH_SNAPSHOT=replay pnpm run test:web` before merge.
